 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(W \cdot H \cdot D \cdot E)$, where $W, H$ are image dimensions, $D$ is the ray depth (diagonal), and $E$ is the number of energy volumes [S1, unofficial]. The inner loop iterates over all energy volumes for each active voxel [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(V + \sum E_i)$, where $V$ is the primary volume size, and $E_i$ are the energy volume sizes [S1, unofficial]. The `colorDictionary` is small [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Strengths:** Allows selective visualization of specific energy types within a structural context defined by the magnitude volume [S1, unofficial]. The thresholding (0.3) reduces noise from low-intensity energy contributions [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Limitations:** The method does not use standard alpha compositing opacity integration; instead, it uses a max-based alpha (`color_a`) and linear blending of colors, which may not preserve physical light transport accuracy [S1, unofficial]. The fixed threshold and color assignment are arbitrary [S1, unofficial].
+- **Time Complexity:** $O(\text{image\_size}^2 \times \text{diagonal} \times N)$, where $N$ is the number of energy volumes.
+- **Memory Complexity:** $O(\text{image\_size}^2)$ for the output image, plus storage for all volume data.
+- **Performance:** Uses a large step size (20) in interactive mode to speed up rendering [S1, unofficial].
+- **Strengths:** Allows visualization of specific energy types within a defined region of interest [S1, unofficial].
+- **Limitations:** Relies on a separate magnitude volume for region definition; thresholding is fixed at 30% [S1, unofficial].
 
